# Visual system

Neon ledger — fun, high-contrast, card-based. Away from monochrome purple SaaS.

## Tokens

Source of truth: `src/styles/tokens.css`, imported via `src/index.css`.

| Mode | Ground | Accents |
|---|---|---|
| Light | Stark white `--paper`, magenta→orange `--header-gradient` on heroes | Hot pink `--flow`, neon category ramp |
| Dark | Deep navy `#1A1A2E`, lifted `--surface-elevated` cards | Electric cyan `--flow`, glowing charts |

Wire into Tailwind v4 `@theme` so `bg-surface`, `text-ink-muted`, `bg-flow`, `text-on-accent` map to tokens.

## Typography

| Role | Face |
|---|---|
| Money figures, page headers | Bricolage Grotesque Variable, weight 700, `letter-spacing: -0.02em` at 44px+ |
| UI, body, labels | Inter Tight |
| Ledger rows, tables | DM Mono |

Rules:

- **Money is the display type.** Dashboard net uses `--t-figure` (44px) or larger, stark white on the gradient header (light) / white on navy (dark).
- Label above figure: `--t-micro`, uppercase, tracked, muted.
- Negative amounts in ledger stay `--ink` unless breached (`--signal`).
- Positive amounts in mixed columns: leading `+` and `--inbound`.

## Component anatomy

### Card (`.card`)
```
border-radius: var(--r-xl);
background: var(--surface);
box-shadow: var(--card-shadow); /* light only */
```
Dark mode: elevated surface, no shadow. One separation method.

### Figure / hero
Light: full-bleed `header-hero` with gradient. Dark: same class, deep navy wash.
Primary number is massive and high-contrast.

### Buttons
Primary: `.btn-primary` or `bg-flow text-on-accent` + optional `--glow-flow`.
Never hardcode `text-white` on accent fills — contrast flips between themes.

### Category row
Glossy emoji icon (`.emoji-icon`) + name + neon progress bar + tabular amount.

### Charts
Neon fills from category tokens. Soft glow (`chart-glow` / per-slice drop-shadow) is allowed.
Custom tooltip matching `.card`. No default Recharts chrome.

## Theme

- `ThemeProvider` + `initTheme()` + inline `index.html` script prevent flash.
- Persist in `localStorage` key `finance-theme`.
- Toggle lives in AppShell chip, More, Settings, Auth.

## Self-check

1. Is the key number the loudest thing on the screen?
2. Do neon accents encode category/state (or primary action), not decoration-for-its-own-sake beyond the approved playful system?
3. Does light use shadow-or-gradient and dark use lifted surfaces correctly?
4. Does it work at 380px without horizontal scroll?
5. Are interactive targets ≥ 44px?
6. Does theme switch update the whole app via tokens?
